    "multirow_9Ahxxk": {
      "type": "multirow",
      "blocks": {
        "row_gittWh": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/dfb1d7fefc64bf9fbaedba7a7d71a5f2_2f1f7f78-c6cb-4e0b-99c3-7577d856b8df.jpg",
            "caption": "",
            "heading": "What we make",
            "text": "<p>Handmade press-on nails — shaped, painted and finished one set at a time by nail artists, never stamped out by the thousand.</p><p>They go on in about ten minutes and come off whenever you decide. No lamp, no drill, no acetone, no appointment. Applied with tabs, a set can be worn again and again, so you can keep several and choose the one that suits where you are going today rather than committing to one look for a month.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "row_pFhMgG": {
          "type": "row",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/e0ebcfd471dfd8a68c983f98b5795137.jpg",
            "caption": "",
            "heading": "Who makes them",
            "text": "<p>Our nails are made by hand by a small group of nail artists in China, most of whom work from home.</p><p>It is deliberate. Skilled nail artists are not hard to find — what is hard to find is a way to sell that skill without a salon chair and fixed hours. Working this way, they set their own schedule and stay with their families, and we get sets painted by people who chose this craft rather than people assigned to a production line. A set someone cared about looks like one.</p><p>Every design is made by our founder alongside them, which is how the standard stays the same whoever picks up the brush.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        },
        "row_6EJyf3": {
          "type": "row",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/6e43225a4e9d5cd2bfbb3f834242b389_7b9de1ac-db4d-469c-adcf-9e7fef464c96.jpg",
            "caption": "",
            "heading": "How a set reaches you",
            "text": "<p>Each set is shaped to follow the curve of a natural nail, built up in layers of professional-grade gel, and finished with every pearl and charm placed by hand.</p><p>Then it gets checked — twice. Once by the studio, once before it is boxed. We are looking for the things that decide whether a set lasts a day or two weeks: smooth edges, embellishments that are properly set, an even finish. Anything that does not pass does not ship.</p><p>Because every set is made by a person, no two are exactly alike. Small differences in tone, in where a pearl sits, in how the light catches the top coat — those are not faults. They are the difference between a print and an original.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": ""
          }
        }
      },
