            "text": "<p>Each one is shaped to follow the curve of a natural nail, built up in layers of professional-grade gel, and finished with every pearl and charm placed by hand.</p><p>Then it is checked twice — once in the studio, once before it is boxed — for the things that decide whether a set lasts a day or two weeks: smooth edges, embellishments properly set, an even finish. Anything that does not pass does not ship.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_mGUKnQ": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What we won't do",
            "text": "<p><strong>No mass production.</strong> Every design is made in small numbers. When a set sells out it may be a while before it returns — sometimes not at all.</p><p><strong>No pretending a machine did it better.</strong> Handmade means small differences in tone, in where a pearl sits, in how the light catches the top coat. That is the difference between a print and an original, and we would rather explain it than iron it out.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_MfX7W7": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Made by women, for women",
            "text": "<p>Everyone who makes these nails is a woman, and most of what we know came from wearing them ourselves — the ones that lifted at the edges after a day, the ones that never quite fit, the ones that were beautiful but wrecked your nails.</p><p>We are building the ones we wanted and could not find.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
